FEATURE: border-color-cycle
DATE: 2026-10-11
SCOPE: let animatedRectangle's colour be tweened; fix animate()'s first frame

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX: two small backwards-compatible changes.
  - animatedRectangle(): lineColor applies on the next frame instead of the next cycle. Code that
    set lineColor mid-run expecting the old delay now sees the colour sooner; nothing else changes.
  - $$.sm().animate(): the first value is never below the start value. Every consumer of animate()
    (core slides do not use it) gets the same curve without the tiny initial dip.

Apps/vilshub.com: the contact-form border fades through #00ffde, #00ff80, #00ff22, #83ff00, #edff00
and back, 2s per colour, using $$.sm(canvas).animate() to tween the colour into
formBorder.config.lineColor. Still single colour under reduced motion.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Headless Chromium on vilshub.com, stroke colour logged per frame for 17s with the form on screen:
reaches #edff00 at ~7.3s and #00ffde again at ~15.7s (four 2s legs each way, 16s round trip),
largest change between consecutive frames 16 per channel, no page errors. Before the core fix the
same run threw "Cannot read properties of undefined" five times and stayed on #00ffde for ~8s.
Not verified: Safari, Firefox.
